---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use | The Açai Club" description="Terms & conditions for using The Açai Club website & services.">

  <section class="pt-28 pb-24 bg-dark min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">

      <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-light mb-4">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="text-grey text-sm mb-12">Last updated: 19 August 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none space-y-8 text-grey leading-relaxed">

        <p>
          These Terms of Use govern your use of theacaiclub.com & our associated ordering platform at theacaiclub.com/order. By using our site, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please stop using our site immediately.
        </p>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">1. Who We Are</h2>
          <p>
            The Açai Club is operated by THE ACAI CLUB, with a registered address at 10a High Street, Datchet, United Kingdom SL3 9EA. Our online ordering platform is provided by EPoS Technologies Limited (Company No. 07122283), 11 Wharf Road, Enfield, EN3 4TA, United Kingdom.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">2. Use of This Website</h2>
          <p>You may use our website for lawful purposes only. You must not:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Use the site in any way that breaches applicable law or regulation</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of our site or systems</li>
            <li>Introduce viruses, malware, or other harmful material</li>
            <li>Reproduce or redistribute content without our express written permission</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">3. Orders & Payment</h2>
          <p>
            All online orders are processed through theacaiclub.com/order. By placing an order, you confirm that the information you provide is accurate & complete.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Payments are processed securely by Stripe. Once an order is confirmed & payment taken, you will not be able to cancel your order. To amend or cancel, please contact your nearest store directly as soon as possible.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Prices displayed are subject to change. We will inform you of any pricing errors before processing your order.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">4. Refunds</h2>
          <p>
            If you believe an item does not meet the description or is of unsatisfactory quality, please contact us. We may request a photograph of the issue. Refunds for online orders will be returned to your original payment method within 5-7 business days. Cash orders must be resolved in-store.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!--
          Gift card + wallet clauses. History matters here, so it is written
          down rather than tidied away.

          ADDED 2026-08-18 for two reasons: an expiry term the customer never
          had a real opportunity to read is CRA 2015 Sch 2 para 10, and under
          s.62 an unfair term is NOT BINDING - so an undisclosed expiry is one
          we could not enforce anyway. And the 14-day cancellation right had
          just been removed from the app FAQ, so this was the only place left
          disclosing it.

          CHANGED 2026-08-19 (T), after the Fable review found the clauses
          described things the code does not do:

          * The 14-day cancellation paragraph is REMOVED, at T's explicit
            instruction, with the consequence put to him first. The RIGHT still
            exists and is still honoured on request - CCR 2013 reg 37(2) does
            not extinguish it until supply has begun and an unspent balance is
            not supply. But reg 31 penalises failing to DISCLOSE it by
            stretching the cancellation window from 14 days to TWELVE MONTHS
            and 14 days, and with nothing disclosed anywhere that is now the
            operative window on every top-up. This is a known, accepted cost,
            not an oversight. Do not re-add the clause without asking T.
          * The unclaimed-gift refund promise is REMOVED: no code ever
            performed it (the 8-week constant had zero consumers), so it
            promised something that did not exist. Refunds are handled on
            request as a support process and are deliberately not advertised.
          * "Your balance can be spent on app and website orders" is now
            app-only. The website has no Add funds screen and never sends
            useWallet, so it cannot spend a balance at all.
          * "A gift card must be added to an account before it can be spent"
            was false: the website spends raw codes in its guest flow. Now
            states both routes.
          * "The expiry date is shown when you buy the card" was false - no
            purchase surface shows a date, only the 12-month period. The date
            is in the recipient's email.

          The 12-month expiry disclosure STAYS, per T: it belongs in the FAQ
          and the legal docs.
        -->        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">5. Gift Cards</h2>
          <p>
            Gift cards are valid for 12 months from the date of purchase. After that date any remaining balance expires and can no longer be spent. The expiry period is shown when you buy the card, and the expiry date is included in the email sent to the recipient.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To spend a gift card in the app it must first be added to an Açai Club account, which is free. A code can also be entered directly at checkout on our website. Gift cards can be spent across as many orders as you like until the balance runs out or the card expires, and are redeemable on app and website orders. They cannot be used in store.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">6. Wallet Balance</h2>
          <p>
            Money you add to your wallet does not expire. You may hold up to £120 at any one time and add up to £120 per day. A gift card added to your wallet keeps its own 12-month expiry from the date that card was bought, so part of your balance may expire while the rest does not.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your balance can be spent on app orders. It is not a payment account, it earns no interest, and it cannot be transferred to another person or exchanged for cash.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">7. Food Allergies</h2>
          <p>
            Our products are prepared in an open kitchen where allergens are handled. While we take precautions, we cannot guarantee that any product is free from allergens due to shared equipment & preparation areas.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you have a serious allergy or intolerance, please contact your nearest store directly before placing an order. See our <a href="/allergens/" class="text-charcoal hover:text-light transition-colors">Allergens page</a> for more information.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">8. Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>
            All content on this website, including text, images, logos & design, is the property of The Açai Club or its licensors. You may not reproduce, distribute, or commercially exploit any content without our express written permission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Açai Club accepts no liability for any loss or damage arising from your use of this website or reliance on any content published here. We make no guarantee that the site will always be available or free from errors.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">10. Run Club &amp; Your Profile</h2>
          <p>
            Our app has a Run Club leaderboard. If you have completed a run with us, you can see it, &amp; you can add a photo to your profile.
          </p>

          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-light mt-6 mb-2">Who sees your photo</h3>
          <p>
            Adding a photo is optional. If you add one, it is shown next to your name on the leaderboard, <strong class="text-light">only to members you have actually run with</strong>. You can hide or delete it at any time in the app. You must be 16 or over to add one.
          </p>

          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-light mt-6 mb-2">What your photo must not contain</h3>
          <p>
            By adding a photo you confirm that it is a photo of you, that it is yours to use, &amp; that it does not contain any of the following:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li>nudity or sexual content</li>
            <li>anything abusive, hateful, or aimed at another person</li>
            <li>a person who is under 16</li>
            <li>anyone other than you, unless they have agreed</li>
            <li>anyone else's phone number, address, or other personal details</li>
            <li>anything that breaks the law or infringes someone else's copyright</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-light mt-6 mb-2">Reporting a photo</h3>
          <p>
            Every profile has a <strong class="text-light">Report</strong> option. Tell us what is wrong &amp; we will look at it <strong class="text-light">within 24 hours</strong>, &amp; usually the same day. You can also <strong class="text-light">Block</strong> another member, which hides you from each other. We do not tell them.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you would rather email, write to <a href="mailto:hello@theacaiclub.com" class="text-light underline">hello@theacaiclub.com</a> &amp; we will treat it the same way.
          </p>

          <h3 class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-light mt-6 mb-2">If we remove your photo</h3>
          <p>
            We will email you to say what we removed &amp; why. <strong class="text-light">You can reply to appeal</strong> &amp; a person, not a machine, will look at it again. If we got it wrong we will put it back. We may remove a photo without warning if it is unlawful.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Repeatedly breaking these rules may mean we stop you adding a photo, or close your account.
          </p>

          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">11. Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Use of our website is also governed by our <a href="/privacy/" class="text-charcoal hover:text-light transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">12. Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of England & Wales. Any disputes shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England & Wales.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-light mb-3">13. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about these Terms, please contact us at:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-1">
            <p>The Açai Club</p>
            <p>10a High Street, Datchet, United Kingdom SL3 9EA</p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@theacaiclub.com" class="text-charcoal hover:text-light transition-colors">hello@theacaiclub.com</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
